1 - \frac{(60 - m)^2}{3600} = 0.4 \implies \frac{(60 - m)^2}{3600} = 0.6 \implies (60 - m)^2 = 2160 \implies 60 - m = \sqrt{2160} \implies m = 60 - \sqrt{2160}
\] Simplifying $\sqrt{2160}$ gives $\sqrt{2160} = \sqrt{36 \times 60} = 6\sqrt{60} = 12\sqrt{15}$. So, $m = 60 - 12\sqrt{15}$. \] <answer> $60 - 12\sqrt{15} $</answer>

